{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511874-infernalism-have-you-ever-traded-soul-in-your-game","id":1511874,"title":"Infernalism - Have you ever traded soul in your game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-17T09:33:27-07:00","id":1511874,"title":"Infernalism - Have you ever traded soul in your game?","content":"I found quite different rule mechanics in the various books that deals with Infernalism. Those presented in &quot;The Path of Screams&quot; are extremely different from those in &quot;Book of Madness&quot;.<br /> Anyway, have you ever experimented with soul trade in your games? Can you tell me some of your stories?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T11:11:49-07:00","id":1512029,"title":"","content":"One player was an infernalist and I must have had a bit too much fun playing the demon. The demon was pushing for her to give more and more of her soul to him, and then she caved and gave the whole thing which was... kind of a downer honestly. She thought I, the storyteller, wanted her to sell but that was entirely in-character and personally I think her character should've lasted much longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T12:35:43-07:00","id":1512037,"title":"","content":"What she got for her soul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T23:33:23-07:00","id":1512088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511874-infernalism-have-you-ever-traded-soul-in-your-game#post1511874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, have you ever experimented with soul trade in your games? Can you tell me some of your stories?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rarely<br /> In my humble opinion, for all tense and purposes, a vampire's soul is a &quot;damaged property&quot;; cursed, damned, tatered, withered remnant of a human soul wich the Shadow/P'o/Beast - call whatever you like - constantly gnaws uppon, and mentaly none of the vampire are &quot;that&quot; stable and more often than not, ends up basically an undead preadtor without any real mind, lands on 0 humanity or dies before that happen.<br /> From purely a darwinian point of view, the neonates/fledlings are basically worthless, an ancille survived long enough to see himself become something he hated during his younger years, and around the time he became an Elder, stopped hating himself for it<br /> Very very very few vampire worth as much as the lowliest human in the eyes of a Demon (demon, not a Fallen, nor a Djin, nor something lowercraftion beyond reality, demon.)<br /> So while the Demon had to have a good reason to enter a pact with a vampire, grant him power, etc, it must have been a darn good reason, so will probably want to keep that vampire... but probbaly would give them a way out for a better deal<br /> A bit like how Jacky boy almost wriggled out from his pact with Davy Jones: 100 human souls for his freedom<br /> <br /> The very few instances when I let my vampire players to sell their soul, it was a monkey paw kind of deal (isn't it always that?) and they really - I mean REALLY had to watch how they word their &quot;wish&quot;, the Pact with very small letters. The devil is in the details... <i>literally </i>(Have you seen Wishmaster?)\u200b<br /> Any Demonologist or Angelologist knows if you asks me to avoid such an investments, or at least make sure to have a way out; like to buy out her share with other souls. <br /> Of course there are other side of the coin, the whole Nergali and other Infernal vampires - but really they never even had a chance to have free will; once they made the deal, they basically lost and just an extension of some entitiy<br /> The only vampire who achieved something with making deals was Ravana who became a Yama King (tho' one can argue, to be a Yama King is not really an achievement...)<br /> <br /> The Thrall-Sebettu relationship is different of course - thats is part of the Game<br /> <br /> Now when it comes to mortals or ghouls? Thats where the fun starts! The Faust and Mephisto dance! <br /> Sadly, as MyWifeIsScary's palyer's case, mine too 99% of the time sell their soul completly... witch is a bit downer, yeah, so never really worth a story - it is wiser to offer them alternatives than infernalism, if you don't want to let htem ruin their character","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T03:49:32-07:00","id":1512107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511874-infernalism-have-you-ever-traded-soul-in-your-game#post1511874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found quite different rule mechanics in the various books that deals with Infernalism. Those presented in &quot;The Path of Screams&quot; are extremely different from those in &quot;Book of Madness&quot;.<br /> Anyway, have you ever experimented with soul trade in your games? Can you tell me some of your stories?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is genuinely a large variety of different kinds of demons in world of darkness. A bane is going to have different pact mechanics than a Fallen, a Yama-King, an Outer Being, a Baali Children, or an Astral Spirit, and all of those are valid forms of &quot;Pact Demons&quot; spread across WoD.<br /> <br /> Demonology is honestly a fun subject to explore, especially in crossover, because of just how much there is to it.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511874-infernalism-have-you-ever-traded-soul-in-your-game?p=1512088#post1512088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very very very few vampire worth as much as the lowliest human in the eyes of a Demon</div> </div> </div> </div>This depends on the type of demon, most don't actually care as far as the books are concerned.<br /> <br /> The only demon breeds that do are 1. Fallen(because vamps have no faith or grace from the abrahamic god) and 2. Yama kings(because they actually bother to measure how much a soul is worth and break it down into sub-currency). To every other species of demon, a soul is a soul and you have to sell the entire thing to have a valid soul-pact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T06:52:09-07:00","id":1512114,"title":"","content":"According to the Book of Madness / Yama kings rules it's fairly easy to just sell a small piece of your soul and go away with some nice benefits and no mechanical drawbacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T14:46:48-07:00","id":1512151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511874-infernalism-have-you-ever-traded-soul-in-your-game?p=1512114#post1512114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the Book of Madness / Yama kings rules it's fairly easy to just sell a small piece of your soul and go away with some nice benefits and no mechanical drawbacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the same book of madness that says a mage loses their avatar and arete permanently after 2*(arete + avatar) years even if they haven't lost any soul points? Read the fine print on that one my dude.<br /> <br /> Yama kings were mentioned in my above post. I definitely wouldn't conflate the two though. Yama Kings don't care about your arete for the same reason they don't care about a wan-kuei's dharmic enlightenment(they're metaphysical beings entirely removed from enlightenment).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 05-19-2023, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T04:46:33-07:00","id":1512205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You mean the same book of madness that says a mage loses their avatar and arete permanently after 2*(arete + avatar) years even if they haven't lost any soul points? Read the fine print on that one my dude. </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I forgot to mention that when I talk about soul trading I always talk about <i>a common mortal</i> , or at best a sorcerer or hedge magician, who engages in soul trading.<br /> ( because, let's face it: if you had the spoiled luck to be one of the Awakened, to engage in soul trade is kinda dumb: just train your own magic instead )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T03:25:22-07:00","id":1513056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511874-infernalism-have-you-ever-traded-soul-in-your-game?p=1512205#post1512205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, I forgot to mention that when I talk about soul trading I always talk about <i>a common mortal</i> , or at best a sorcerer or hedge magician, who engages in soul trading.<br /> ( because, let's face it: if you had the spoiled luck to be one of the Awakened, to engage in soul trade is kinda dumb: just train your own magic instead )</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but it also depends a lot on which soul-trading playbook you get to deal with. If you are an Awakened mage, engaging in soul trade (or for that matter, becoming a ghoul) to any degree under Book of Madness (or Blood Treachery) rules is extremely dumb. You might as well slit your throat while your Avatar is still intact and bound to you. On the other hand, if you get to make a reasonable amount of deals with generic demons under Path of Screams or Book of the Fallen rules or with the Fallen under Devil's Due rules, you can harness a considerable amount of additional power through appropriate Investments/Arcana to supplement your Foundation/Arete and Pillars/Spheres at no real harm for your Awakened powers. Sure, you shall get extra Taints/Flaws and/or have to do nasty deeds to pay for the stuff, and you have to manage your relationship with your patron, but this is par the course. No matter how much Phil Brucato likes to be verbose on the issue, fact is moral issues about this are only relevant to certain characters and players, esp. without Karma meters to enforce them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 05-28-2023, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T08:30:08-07:00","id":1513197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511874-infernalism-have-you-ever-traded-soul-in-your-game?p=1512205#post1512205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, I forgot to mention that when I talk about soul trading I always talk about <i>a common mortal</i> , or at best a sorcerer or hedge magician, who engages in soul trading.<br /> ( because, let's face it: if you had the spoiled luck to be one of the Awakened, to engage in soul trade is kinda dumb: just train your own magic instead )</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. Personally thought that the Book of Madness demon lord only dealt with mages.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, anyone can get paradox-free awakened magic by the book's rules(the &quot;infernal magic&quot; investment).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T13:33:58-07:00","id":1513228,"title":"","content":"Players don't want to give control to the ST, and infernalist investmentsare just the worst way to lose control of your agency. I've found it more interesting to use actual narrative challenges and temptations to let them doom themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T14:51:30-07:00","id":1513234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511874-infernalism-have-you-ever-traded-soul-in-your-game?p=1513228#post1513228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Players don't want to give control to the ST, and infernalist investments are just the worst way to lose control of your agency. I've found it more interesting to use actual narrative challenges and temptations to let them doom themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is both true and false at the same time.<br /> <br /> Infernal investments are a system designed to make a character lose agency, but they're also designed to have enough wiggle room that Some people can come out on top. This is also by design, the devil isn't going to have many customers if Everyone loses, but like the lottery or gambling in general, a 0.1% chance of getting everything you dreamed of is enough to motivate a customer base.<br /> <br /> TTRPG players Also tend to like to gambling, which should be rather unsurprising considering we're playing what amounts to a dice gambling game with a focus on role-play. So infernal investments, if played with care, can actually make for really good stories of both the triumphant &quot;king solomon&quot; or classic greek tragedy variety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T16:39:26-07:00","id":1513341,"title":"","content":"Not so much soul trade as giving it away. My first VtM character was largely based on Felicity Latimer from Bill Garnett's novel <i>Down-bound Train</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T07:06:01-07:00","id":1513390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511874-infernalism-have-you-ever-traded-soul-in-your-game?p=1513234#post1513234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is both true and false at the same time.<br /> <br /> Infernal investments are a system designed to make a character lose agency, but they're also designed to have enough wiggle room that Some people can come out on top. This is also by design, the devil isn't going to have many customers if Everyone loses, but like the lottery or gambling in general, a 0.1% chance of getting everything you dreamed of is enough to motivate a customer base.<br /> <br /> TTRPG players Also tend to like to gambling, which should be rather unsurprising considering we're playing what amounts to a dice gambling game with a focus on role-play. So infernal investments, if played with care, can actually make for really good stories of both the triumphant &quot;king solomon&quot; or classic greek tragedy variety.</div> </div> </div> </div>You must have drastically different players than the people I've played with. In my experience people are allergic to being indebted or serving anyone. And gambling, jesus, just selling people on swingy systems is enough to have them break out in hives. Players are willing to risk things, but it's all about making sure they know what they're getting into and making sure they are ready for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T03:23:58-07:00","id":1513854,"title":"","content":"I played in a KotE game and engaged in a bit of soul trading with a Yama King. The local Mandarin was an Akuma serving Emma-O. My character needed to get proof but was unable to do so. So my character ended up engaging in some soul trade with Mikaboshi, selling couple pieces of her soul in order to get the proof that she needed. She justified it as doing it &quot;for the greater good&quot; - she sold a small piece of her soul and in exchange managed to get an Akuma in a high ranking position killed. And becoming a hero of the court for uncovering the truth and all of the rewards that came with it were, well, she was more than happy to take them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T15:41:31-07:00","id":1514347,"title":"","content":"Not really, but a player, who had older World of Darkness books (1st-edition), talked about Dark Vestments which, well, I just assumed it was from an older edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T05:50:45-07:00","id":1514453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511874-infernalism-have-you-ever-traded-soul-in-your-game?p=1514347#post1514347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, but a player, who had older World of Darkness books (1st-edition), talked about Dark Vestments which, well, I just assumed it was from an older edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure vestments are a thing from chronicles, not classic WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T05:59:46-07:00","id":1514456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511874-infernalism-have-you-ever-traded-soul-in-your-game?p=1514347#post1514347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, but a player, who had older World of Darkness books (1st-edition), talked about Dark Vestments which, well, I just assumed it was from an older edition.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Storytellers Handbook to the Sabbat </b>(1993 edition) had the Demonic Investments<br /> <br /> Level One<br /> Aquatic - the Infernalist can swim underwater as fast as he can run. With a slightly aquatic look. If mortal, he will gain gills.<br /> Bat Ears - the Infernalist will gain same abilities as a bat's sonar.<br /> Body Armor - this can be used 5 times to take less damage.<br /> Grim Jaws - the Infernalist receives the ability to chew through anything. And can swallow objects up to the size of a small child. The facial features are normal unless using this power.<br /> Kiss of Hades - the Infernalist can cause aggravated damage with the touch of his lips. The victim must first be grabbed or surprised.<br /> Lashing Tail - the Infernalist grows a small tail which may be used to cause aggravated damage like a whip. The tail must be hidden or everyone will know you are an Infernalist.<br /> Magic Sense - allows the Infernalist to sense any use of magic within 500 yrs of herself. The Infernalist must concentrate to use this and it will reveal no discipline other than Thaumaturgy.<br /> Razor Fangs - increases the sharpness and size of the Infernalist's fangs allowing aggravated damage when used. Costs one blood point.<br /> Razor Fingers - identical to Razor Fangs only with fingernails.<br /> Smell Fear - the Infernalist will detect by scent if anyone is afraid within 100 feet.<br /> <br /> Level Two<br /> Invisibility to Animals - the Infernalist will be unseen to animals though some may still smell her. They will cower in fright from the Infernalist.<br /> Pheromone Powers - gives Infernalists pheromones that make all mortals within 30 feet easier to Dominate.<br /> Psychic Tracker - infernalist can track someone and know when they are near their target. Does not give precise location. Cost 1 blood point per hour.\u200b<br /> <br /> Level Three<br /> Cause Vertigo - the victim's will have problems staying upright, mortals will suffer nausea. Can be used against any number of people at 1 blood point a person. Last 5 turns.<br /> Magic Portal - allows the Infernalist to move through solid objects. Cost 1 blood point.<br /> Walk the Walls - the Infernalist can walk on walls or ceilings at a walk or crawl.<br /> Demon Hide - alters the Infernalist's skin, allowing two damage soak and causing fire damage to any piercing item. incidentally this also allows fire damage to claws or biting.\u200b<br /> <br /> Level Four<br /> Guardian - the Infernalist will receive an imp for protector. The imp will serve her and have an empathic tie so that they will know the location and emotional state of each other.<br /> Toxic Blast - the Infernalist can spew a liquid of demonic energy from their nose, eyes, mouth or fingertips. It will disappear 5 turns after it spurts. This is a hideous smelling, acidic, blackish green goo. Costs 1 blood point for one blast that will cause aggravated damage.<br /> Two Dimensional - the Infernalist will become two dimensional allowing him to slip through cracks and become almost nonexistent when viewed from the side. Cost 1 blood point.\u200b<br /> <br /> Level Five<br /> Hell Skinned - grants the Infernalist immunity from the fire and heat. But not from sunlight or magic fire.<br /> Life Leech - the Infernalist can drain the Willpower of mortals, ghouls, and werewolves, turning the points drained into blood points. Touching is required. Victims completely drained will become catatonic until they gain more Willpower.<br /> Master of the Domain - the Infernalist will always know what is happening 500 feet inside of her domain as if they were watching from above.\u200b<br /> <br /> Level Six<br /> Atrophic Touch - will cause one of victim's arms or legs to wither away to nothing. There is no pain but the limb will disappear. The Infernalist must touch the body part to be effected.<br /> Teleportation - at a cost of 1 blood point and 1 Willpower, the Infernalist can use this to go from one place to another within 100 feet. The destination does not have to be seen.<br /> Turn to Toad - the power to turn a victim into a toad. Lasts 1 night per success and costs 1 Blood Point and 1 Willpower.\u200b<br /> <br /> Level Seven<br /> Infernal Passage - grants safe passage through Hell. This can only be given by extremely powerful demons. Does not give the Infernalist passage to Hell.<br /> Journey to the Spirit Realm - the Infernalist's body becomes a spirit to travel through the Umbra at 1 Blood Point per hour of travel.<br /> Summon Hellions - 3 minor demons can be summoned by the Infernalist to protect her from danger. The demons will not put themselves in danger but will try to protect the Infernalist. Costs 1 Blood Point to use.<br /> <br /> Level Eight<br /> Army of the Damned - 9 minor demons can be summoned by the Infernalist to protect her from danger. They will fight until their forms are destroyed. Costs 1 Blood Point.<br /> <br /> Level Nine<br /> Infernal Ranking - gives the Infernalist minor status among the damned. The Infernalist is superior to minor demons and can command them. They cannot be forced but most will obey as punishing disobedience is acceptable and expected.<br /> <br /> Level Ten<br /> Rejuvenation - this will allow an Infernalist to permanently transform back to mortal capable of aging normally. The Infernalist becomes unembraceable and if it is forced will probably die.\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200bBut<b> Infernalism: The Path of Screams </b>(an 1998 supplement to the Mage: The Sorcerers Crusade setting) and the 1994 <b> Book of Madness </b>had a fair shair of theim too, but those were not really cainite specific, while the Sabbat ones, obviously were - tho' Demons, so, anything could fly, storytellers descretion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Demonic Investments are not super-powers, nor are they employed easily. Most require an invocation to the Patronus and some physical effort. When a Fallen One uses an Investment, their aura turns dark red, then black; anyone with mystic senses (Gifts, spells, Disciplines and so forth, as well as the Awareness Talent) can tell that dark forces are at work in his vicinity. Even mortals feel deep chills. Most Investments actually transform the lnfernalist, too; a diabolist with Wings actually sprouts skeletal bat-wings from their back! <br /> When one enters into a pact with a demon, the demon will give investments, wealth, personal service, objects of desire, and more. The power of an investment is with the demon not the receiver of the investment. A vampire with even one investment will have a devil's mark<br /> Whether or not the pact is observed, the demon eventually collects its due and the Infernalist joins her master in Hell...<br /> (If an Infernalist is foolish enough to make a pact then break it, her Investments disappear immediately and the chase begins. In game terms, a bargaining Infernalist gains character points \u2013 points he/she can spend on Backgrounds and Investments. Such powers fail on Christmas Day, Easter and Beltane (and, in the Middle East, during Ramadan), when Divine might banishes the Darkness from the Earth...)<br /> <br /> Could be an interesting game, but oh boy, a headache<br /> Players always - <i>always</i> - sell their souls then.. well... you can guess it how it ends <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T15:46:04-07:00","id":1514627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511874-infernalism-have-you-ever-traded-soul-in-your-game?p=1514456#post1514456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Storytellers Handbook to the Sabbat </b>(1993 edition) had the Demonic Investments</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're talking about &quot;Dark Vestments&quot;, an actual thing in CofD dealing with the powers of beings possessed by demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T22:51:20-07:00","id":1514654,"title":"","content":"Not considered it, because it is a CofD thing, but you are right<br /> oWoD as far as I know don't have Vestments... well except Vestment of Vileness, an artifact from Players Guide to the Sabbat <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The closest to it are the Fomorian powers amd the Demonic Investments<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T02:00:25-07:00","id":1514670,"title":"","content":"Honestly, in terms of rules oWoD Infernalism is quite a mess - probably due to how the idea was there but every edition and sub-line handled it differently. Couple that with the different lore the diverse 'hells' in the setting have and it becomes pretty obvious it's badly in need of a clean-up. I don't know if it's better in CofD, but I can't imagine it to be worse.<br /> <br /> I generally like the idea of Investments better than just unlocking a new discipline or Thauma Path and I think that the relationship between a character and their patron should mechanically more resemble that between Fera and Spirits (specifically a Totem). I would probably also separate 'infernal' and 'chthonic/eldritch' as functional categories similar to Thaumaturgy and Necromancy just to make sense of the lore behind some of the powers - like Nergali Baali vs Molochim, or how Abyss Mysticism is different from Dark Thauma.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T12:51:28-07:00","id":1514739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511874-infernalism-have-you-ever-traded-soul-in-your-game?p=1514670#post1514670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, in terms of rules oWoD Infernalism is quite a mess - probably due to how the idea was there but every edition and sub-line handled it differently. Couple that with the different lore the diverse 'hells' in the setting have and it becomes pretty obvious it's badly in need of a clean-up. I don't know if it's better in CofD, but I can't imagine it to be worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly believe the mess is intentional. Like you said yourself, there is a diverse array of hells and demon types with nothing to do with each other. Giving a &quot;clean&quot; list of powers common to every single one would conflict with the established setting.<br /> <br /> It also serves a purpose. Infernalism is Supposed to make you feel like you're out of your depth and unsure of what exactly you made a deal with. It's an unfair system designed to ensure as many people Lose as possible while still being incredibly tempting to the eyes of outsiders who may be partial to &quot;trying their luck&quot;. Having it not be straight forward and poorly balanced is actually better in line with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511874-infernalism-have-you-ever-traded-soul-in-your-game?p=1514670#post1514670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally like the idea of Investments better than just unlocking a new discipline or Thauma Path and I think that the relationship between a character and their patron should mechanically more resemble that between Fera and Spirits (specifically a Totem). I would probably also separate 'infernal' and 'chthonic/eldritch' as functional categories similar to Thaumaturgy and Necromancy just to make sense of the lore behind some of the powers - like Nergali Baali vs Molochim, or how Abyss Mysticism is different from Dark Thauma.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are though? On a meta level.<br /> <br /> For example: Fallen demons specifically aren't the same thing banes, &quot;the children&quot;, neverborn, high umbral demon, etc. They all have different &quot;Deal&quot; systems because they aren't the same creatures.<br /> <br /> In character, it makes sense no one knows the difference because the academic nuance of what creature you're dealing with is entirely outside the ability of most factions to know. So everything is labled a &quot;demon&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T13:19:59-07:00","id":1514746,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I can only partially agree. From a ST perspective, having a coherent (or at least as coherent as the WoD gets) background and system makes it easier for me to juggle it. For example, I think converting the various Necromancy Disciplines into a Blood Sorcery Path was a good decision that doesn't take away from the individuality of the different practitioners. I do agree with keeping the various sources distinct, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T16:32:23-07:00","id":1514779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1511874-infernalism-have-you-ever-traded-soul-in-your-game?p=1514746#post1514746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I can only partially agree. From a ST perspective, having a coherent (or at least as coherent as the WoD gets) background and system makes it easier for me to juggle it. For example, I think converting the various Necromancy Disciplines into a Blood Sorcery Path was a good decision that doesn't take away from the individuality of the different practitioners. I do agree with keeping the various sources distinct, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, WoD one of those game where user-friendly tools for the ST come secondary to the experience of the player.<br /> <br /> Look me in the eye and tell me this game isn't a hot mess, or that it isn't an even <i>More</i> unholy mess in crossover(so much so that even the Devs gave up and changed the default of &quot;One world of Darkness&quot; to a &quot;Many Worlds&quot; setting in the transition from second to revised).<br /> <br /> I still love it to bits though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T03:43:42-07:00","id":1515844,"title":"","content":"I once briefly played an infernalist technocrat based on Dr betruger and Dr pierce in Doom. She didn't pact with the demons as in exchange her investments where rewards for sincere service, she saw the demons as lovecraftian aliens who existed beyond our limited understanding and service to them would enlighten and uplift her and mankind....and if not we'll its just the natural order of things isn't it? <br /> <br /> Evil and crazy. The only pacts she had were that her corruption couldn't be detected by most forms of magic and psychic defences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T08:25:10-07:00","id":1515867,"title":